what is the 50 30 20 rule

AI:
The 50/30/20 rule is a simple budgeting framework:

  50% — Needs (rent, groceries, transport, utilities)
  30% — Wants (gaming, cinema, gym, café, dining out)
  20% — Savings and debt repayment

Example with $2,500 income:
  $1,250 → needs
  $750   → wants (Xbox, MCine, Maison de Thé, gym)
  $500   → savings

It is a guideline not a strict rule. But it helps people see if they are spending too much in one area. With your user spending over $1,000 on wants (Gaming + Cinema + Tea) out of a $2,500 income, they are above the 30% wants limit.

